{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Problem\n\nThe live prompt-eval loop in `.github/workflows/prompt-eval.yml` (`eval-live`) calls `rebar.llm.evals.eval.run_eval` on every dataset-bearing spec under `src/rebar/llm/eval_specs/`. Three of those specs have no solver, so every case is recorded as a run error and the spec reports coverage 0.00:\n\n| spec | cases (at `REBAR_EVAL_MAX_CASES=12`, 3 epochs) | message |\n|---|---|---|\n| plan-review-container | 36 | `run error: no eval solver for prompt 'plan-review-container'` |\n| plan-review-finder | 36 | `run error: no eval solver for prompt 'plan-review-finder'` |\n| plan-review-isf-finder | 12 | `run error: no eval solver for prompt 'plan-review-isf-finder'` |\n\nThe error is raised at the end of `run_case` (`src/rebar/llm/evals/eval_solver.py:423`) after no prompt-id branch matches.\n\n## Root cause (measured 2026-11-17, origin/main 05c6414358f)\n\n`run_case` resolves a plan-review spec to a solver only through `_criterion_id(prompt_id)` (`eval_solver.py:76`), which strips `plan-review-` and looks the remainder up in the criterion registry. These three specs are named after the PASS prompts, not a criterion (`passes.PASS_FINDER`, `PASS_CONTAINER`, `PASS_ISF` at `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/passes.py:140,150,151`), so `finder`, `container` and `isf-finder` resolve to nothing. The data is runnable:\n\n- `plan-review-finder` (37 cases) and `plan-review-container` (12 cases) carry a per-case `criterion` field; every value resolves in `registry.by_id` (checked: 0 unresolved), and every container case (G3/G4) carries the `children` payload `_run_criterion_case` needs (`eval_solver.py:101`).\n- `plan-review-isf-finder` (4 cases) carries inline `log` and `plan` text, which is exactly the input of `passes.pass1_isf(runner, cfg, *, plan, session_log_text)` (`passes.py:417`), a single non-agentic structured call.\n\n## Approach\n\nAdd the missing dispatch to `run_case`, reusing the production pass functions so the eval scores the same code path the gate runs:\n\n1. Pass-finder arm: when `prompt_id` is `passes.PASS_FINDER` or `passes.PASS_CONTAINER`, read the case's `criterion`, resolve it with `_criterion_id`, and run `_run_criterion_case` for it (which already routes container criteria to `pass1_container` and the rest to `pass1_chunk`). A case without a resolvable `criterion` raises `ValueError` naming the case id, so it is a visible run error, never a silent pass.\n2. ISF arm: when `prompt_id` is `passes.PASS_ISF`, a new `_run_isf_case` calls `passes.pass1_isf` with the case's `plan` and `log` under `resolve_gate_config(repo_root)` and returns `{\"findings\": [...]}`. A case missing `plan` or `log` raises `ValueError`.\n3. Both arms sit with the other exact-id arms (novelty/verifier), before the criterion arm.\n\n`INLINE_UNADMISSIBLE_CRITERIA` is unchanged: an `input`-only ISF fixture (sidecar replay) still cannot run, because it has no log. No config key, env var or flag is added.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/llm/evals/eval_solver.py` — the two arms, `_run_isf_case`, docstrings.\n- `tests/unit/test_eval_solver.py` — offline tests with `FakeRunner`.\n- `tests/unit/test_provider_parity.py` — correct the docstring of `test_the_isf_finder_spec_is_excluded_because_it_resolves_to_no_arm` (`:404`), which states `run_case` has no arm for the spec; its assertions (no PARITY arm) stay unchanged.\n\nPortability: no subprocess, file descriptor, signal or path handling is added; the arms are pure in-process dispatch.\n\n## Testing\n\nOffline with `FakeRunner` (no model):\n- happy path: a finder case (`criterion: T2`) and a container case (`criterion: G3`, `children`) from the packaged specs run and return a `findings` list; an ISF case with `plan`/`log` returns the canned finding attributed `criteria == [\"ISF\"]`;\n- failure path: a finder case with no `criterion`, and an ISF case with no `log`, raise `ValueError`.\n- end to end: `run_eval` over each of the three specs with a solve that delegates to `run_case` with a `FakeRunner` reports `coverage == 1.0`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `run_case` resolves `plan-review-finder`, `plan-review-container` and `plan-review-isf-finder` cases to a solver; checked by `tests/unit/test_eval_solver.py`, where `run_eval` over each packaged spec with a `FakeRunner`-backed solve reports `coverage == 1.0`.\n- [ ] A finder/container case without a resolvable `criterion`, and an ISF case without `log`, raise `ValueError` naming the problem; checked by unit tests.\n- [ ] Genuinely unknown prompt ids still raise \"no eval solver\" (existing `test_unknown_prompt_raises` passes).\n- [ ] `make verify` exits 0.\n"}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1794969376816066828,"uuid":"0bfd3e95-8962-4c80-8134-1a9f36b33f8d"}